 "▼ Dive in: <0>Penalties</0>": "",
 "<0>Logprobs</0> are natural logs of token probabilities. Summing them over a reply gives how likely the model found that whole text; APIs can return them.": "",
 "<0>Penalties</0> (repetition, frequency, presence) lower the logits of tokens already seen, discouraging loops.": "",
 "<0>Constrained decoding</0> masks logits of tokens that would break a grammar or JSON schema to −∞, so output is guaranteed to parse.": "",
 "logprob = ln p. p = {#} → {#}; p = {#} → {#}. Perplexity = exp(−mean logprob).": "",
 "Constrained decoding works by editing logits before softmax; the model itself is unchanged. See <0>valid JSON</0> for how tool calls use it.": "",
 "Penalty formulas vary between providers; the ones shown are common textbook forms.": "",
